This guard is meant to stop path traversal. Which input gets past it?

```js
const base = '/srv/uploads';
const target = path.resolve(base, userPath);
if (!target.startsWith(base)) throw new Error('forbidden');
return fs.createReadStream(target);
```

What is printed, and with which exit code does the process end?

```js
process.on('exit', (code) => {
  setTimeout(() => console.log('cleanup done'), 0);
  console.log('exit handler', code);
});
process.exitCode = 7;
```

What does this print?

```js
let n = 0;
process.on('beforeExit', () => {
  console.log('beforeExit', n);
  if (n++ < 2) setTimeout(() => {}, 1);
});
process.on('exit', (c) => console.log('exit', c));
```

Put the console output of this script in order.

```js
process.on('exit', () => console.log('exit'));
process.on('beforeExit', () => console.log('beforeExit'));
setTimeout(() => console.log('timer'), 10);
console.log('main end');
```

A CLI starts a background updater and should then exit immediately:

```js
spawn(process.execPath, ['updater.js'], { detached: true, stdio: 'ignore' });
console.log('update started');
```

The CLI prints the message but hangs until the updater finishes. Why?
